---
// The High Tea package page - the third of the three meal formats, an
// afternoon alternative to the formal banquet (the catalogue's own framing).
// Three tiers (Jasmine, Hibiscus, Tulip), built to the same pattern as
// reception-package.html: same tier switcher, same sticky switcher, same
// .package-menu-* markup, same shared chrome. Linked from the High Tea card
// in weddings.html's packages section.
//
// Per-person prices (35/45/55 euro) come from the client's own shared quote,
// not from the catalogue - the catalogue's menu pages carry no prices at all.
// Unlike Banquet, there is no conflicting second source for these, so they
// are shown. Treat them as one data point rather than a fixed rate card: the
// client has said pricing is generated internally and varies by season.
//
// NO (V) MARKERS ANYWHERE ON THIS PAGE, deliberately, and this is surfaced to
// the reader rather than left silent: the catalogue marks vegetarian items
// throughout Reception and Banquet but not once across Jasmine, Hibiscus or
// Tulip. A .package-menu-note-warning callout under the tier cards says so
// and says why we haven't inferred markers from dish names - getting that
// wrong mislabels a dish to a guest with a dietary requirement, which is a
// worse failure than an absent marker. The allergen callout at the foot of
// the page therefore also has its "(V) vegetarian." legend line removed,
// since there are no badges for it to explain. Restore both the legend line
// and the badges together, once Bacchus confirms which items qualify.
//
// Content is taken from docs/bacchus-wedding-catalogue.pdf, read from the
// rendered pages rather than from extracted text. An automated text pull of
// this PDF silently drops every accented character and, in places, whole
// words - "Goat's Cheese" vanished from one Orchid line, "Gavi Di Gavi" from
// a wine name. Do not rebuild these lists from a text extraction.
//
// Capitalisation and spelling follow reception-package.html's existing
// house-style normalisation rather than the catalogue's own inconsistencies,
// which is the convention that page already set. Corrections applied, listed
// here so the client can confirm or reverse them: "SANWHICHES" to
// "Sandwiches", "SAVORIES" to "Savouries", "Caramelized" to "Caramelised",
// "Pine Not Roll" to "Pine Nut Roll", "Macaroons" to "Macarons" (the
// catalogue's own Stations page says "Macaron Tower"), and sentence-cased
// dish words raised to title case.
//
// This page carries NO signature-dish photo tiles, unlike
// reception-package.html. That component captions each tile with a specific
// dish name, and no per-dish photography exists for this package - a stand-in
// under a real dish name would be a false claim rather than a placeholder.
// Imagery is deliberately BLACKED OUT rather than filled with stand-in
// photography, on request: the hero is a flat black .hero-media with a
// labelled chip over it, and each tier leads with three
// .package-dish-placeholder tiles - black, dashed oxblood border, the dish's
// initials and a "photo to follow" line. None of them can be opened; there is
// nothing to enlarge, so the page has no lightbox. A stand-in photo reads as
// a finished choice in a walkthrough, whereas an empty black frame reads as
// "still to come", which is the honest signal while the client sources
// images. The carousel further down is the exception and does use real
// generic Bacchus photography, labelled as such in its own lead.
//
// To swap real imagery in: put an <img> back inside .hero-media (see
// reception-package.html) and drop .package-hero-placeholder; replace each
// .package-dish-placeholder with .gallery-item/.gallery-tag markup and copy
// the page-scoped lightbox controller back from reception-package.html.
//
import BaseLayout from "@layouts/BaseLayout.astro"
import { HIGH_TEA_TIERS } from "@data/packages/high-tea"
import PackageTierSection from "@components/packages/PackageTierSection.astro"
import PackageMenuNote from "@components/packages/PackageMenuNote.astro"
import PageHero from "@components/sections/PageHero.astro"
import EnquirySection from "@components/enquiry/EnquirySection.astro"
import WaitlistPopover from "@components/enquiry/WaitlistPopover.astro"
import ArrowIcon from "@components/ui/ArrowIcon.astro"
import PhotoCarousel from "@components/sections/PhotoCarousel.astro"
// After BaseLayout, so these load after global.css (see package-page.css).
import "@styles/package-page.css"
import "@styles/package-dish-placeholders.css"

// The "closer look" photo strip.
const carouselSlides = [
  {
    src: "food-and-drink/canapes-service",
    alt: "A waiter serving canapés at a wedding reception",
    caption: "Canapés, Passed",
  },
  {
    src: "venue/terrace-celebration-reception",
    alt: "Guests mingling at a Bacchus wedding reception on the Terrace",
    caption: "Guests, On the Terrace",
  },
  {
    src: "food-and-drink/champagne",
    alt: "A guest raising a glass of sparkling wine at a dressed table",
    caption: "A Toast, On Arrival",
  },
  {
    src: "venue/terrace-marquee-tables",
    alt: "Tables dressed under a marquee on the Terrace",
    caption: "The Terrace, Dressed",
  },
  {
    src: "venue/secret-garden-night",
    alt: "A long candlelit table in the Secret Garden at night",
    caption: "The Secret Garden, By Night",
  },
]
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Our High Tea Menus — Bacchus"
  menuBackgroundImage="weddings/cake-chandelier"
>
  <PageHero crumb="High Tea Menus" parent={{ href: "/weddings", label: "Weddings" }}>
    Our High Tea <em>Menus</em>
    <Fragment slot="sub">
      Dainty sandwiches, hot savouries and a table of sweets — an afternoon alternative to
      the formal banquet.
    </Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="sub-secondary">
      Three considered tiers, each explored in full below.
    </Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="ctas">
      <a href="#enquire" class="button button-gradient button-shimmer">
        <span>Book a tasting</span>
        <ArrowIcon />
      </a>
      <a
        href="/docs/bacchus-wedding-catalogue.pdf"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener"
        class="button button-ghost"
      >
        <span>View the catalogue</span>
      </a>
    </Fragment>
  </PageHero>

  <PackageTierSection tiers={HIGH_TEA_TIERS}>
    <Fragment slot="heading">
      Compare the three <em>tiers</em>
    </Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="lead">
      <p class="lead">
        Jasmine, Hibiscus and Tulip are three readings of the same afternoon table, each
        more generous than the last.
      </p>
      <p class="lead">
        Switch between them below — every item is taken straight from the printed
        catalogue.
      </p>
    </Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="after-cards">
      <PackageMenuNote variant="warning">
        <p>
          <b>Vegetarian marking is missing from the High Tea menus.</b>
        </p>
        <p>
          The printed catalogue marks vegetarian items (V) throughout the Reception and
          Banquet menus, but not once across Jasmine, Hibiscus or Tulip. We have
          reproduced it as received rather than inferring markers from dish names, which
          would risk mislabelling a dish to a guest with a dietary requirement.
        </p>
        <p>
          Bacchus caters for vegetarian, vegan and gluten-free requirements — please raise
          them with the team, and we will add the markers here once confirmed.
        </p>
      </PackageMenuNote>
    </Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="after-panels">
      <PackageMenuNote>
        <p>
          Menu items may contain or come into contact with allergens — please discuss
          requirements with the Bacchus sales team.
        </p>
        <p>
          BCL is certified Halal by The World Islamic Call Society (Malta Branch). Full
          terms are in the printed catalogue.
        </p>
      </PackageMenuNote>
      <div class="package-stations-note" data-reveal style="--d: 60ms">
        <p>
          Comparing formats? Also see our{" "}
          <a href="/weddings/packages/reception" class="link-underline-inline">
            Reception
          </a>{" "}
          and{" "}
          <a href="/weddings/packages/banquet" class="link-underline-inline">
            Banquet
          </a>{" "}
          menus.
        </p>
      </div>
    </Fragment>
  </PackageTierSection>

  <section class="section-padding">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div class="eyebrow" id="closerLookEyebrow" data-reveal>
          From the High Tea
        </div>
        <h2 data-reveal style="--d: 80ms">
          A closer look, in <em>five</em> frames
        </h2>
        <p class="lead" data-reveal style="--d: 160ms; margin-top: 22px">
          Drag, swipe or use the arrows. Generic Bacchus photography for now — easily
          swapped for shots of the High Tea itself once available.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <PhotoCarousel slides={carouselSlides} />
  </section>

  <EnquirySection
    eventType="Wedding"
    railPhoto={{
      src: "celebrations/tea-pour",
      alt: "A guest pouring tea at an outdoor garden celebration",
      caption: "Tea poured in the garden.",
    }}
  >
    <Fragment slot="heading">
      Tell us about your <em>wedding</em>
    </Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="lead">
      Four short steps. We come back with dates, pricing and a proposal shaped to your day
      — before we ever get on the phone.
    </Fragment>
  </EnquirySection>

  <WaitlistPopover slot="after-footer" />

  <script>
    import "@scripts/package-tiers.js"
  </script>
</BaseLayout>
